WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Pair the reference and blurred candidate on the same three-dimensional grid, using gain one.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Compute positive local contrast by subtracting a 0.4 millimetre Gaussian background.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Use only the reference to identify tubular support, then split it into weak and strong contrast groups.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Measure shared contrast in each group. Q is 100 times the geometric mean of the two overlap scores.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Q complements PSNR, full-image SSIM and L1. The three controls retain background and structural changes separately.

